            <ArticleTitle>[Neurological symptoms with a hepatitis E virus infection].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>D107</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND">Infection with hepatitis E virus genotype 3 (HEV3) is an emerging zoonosis in the industrialized world. The infection usually proceeds asymptomatically. Extrahepatic sequelae including neurological symptoms have been described.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CASE DESCRIPTION">A 52-year-old man presented at the emergency department with pain, muscle weakness and sensory disorders in both shoulders and arms. He was found to have bilateral neuralgic amyotrophy accompanying an HEV3 infection.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION">An HEV3 infection can have neurological sequelae, but very little is known about its incidence and spectrum of symptoms.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
